Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Settings and shared definitions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f65b29e5-9165-45e2-a0fa-21da6569f279"],

Cell["\<\
Settings for all figures and tables, as in the main notebook. figFont and \
tabFont set the font sizes of every figure and every table; wFull and wHalf \
keep every figure inside an A4 page when the notebook is printed or saved as \
PDF. logLine and logText draw reference lines and labels on log-log plots.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fbe5e47e-6c07-473c-b8e2-779feb7fbdfc"],

Cell["\<\
(*c.0*)
figFont = 14;   (* font size in figures and diagrams *)
tabFont = 10;   (* font size in tables *)
wFull = 440;    (* full figure width in points; A4 text width is ~487 *)
wHalf = 215;    (* width of each panel in a two-column figure *)
figStyle = Directive[Black, FontSize -> figFont];
table[rows_, label_] := Labeled[
   Grid[rows, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left,
    BaseStyle -> {FontSize -> tabFont}, Spacings -> {0.8, 0.5},
    Background -> {None, {1 -> GrayLevel[0.92]}}],
   Style[label, Bold, FontSize -> tabFont + 1], Top];
panel[opts___] :=
  Sequence[opts, LabelStyle -> figStyle, ImageSize -> wHalf];
figure[rows_, label_] := Labeled[Grid[rows], Style[label, figFont], Top];
sci[x_] := ScientificForm[x, 2];
(* reference lines and labels on log-log plots, given in plot units *)
logLine[pts_] := {Gray, Dashed, Line[Log[N[pts]]]};
logText[str_, pt_] := Text[Style[str, figFont - 2, Gray], Log[N[pt]]];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"eb1cb40d-74ce-4567-bbab-e9ccf06baa83"],

Cell["\<\
Example A of the main notebook, f(x) = sin(2\[Pi]x) + x\.b2/2, and a \
vectorized version of the staircase of Eq. (M7) that accepts any S-shape. The \
last line checks it against stair of cell c.8 of the main notebook; the \
difference is at the level of rounding.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"748986b3-349b-4e0c-9f53-b328a57246b7"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(*c.0.1*)
(* example A of the main notebook, section 4 *)
f[x_] := Sin[2 Pi x] + x^2/2;
(* the staircase of Eq. (M7) for any S-shape s, on a list of points xs;
   vals = values of the target at the nodes 0, 1/N, ..., 1 *)
stairOn[s_, vals_, lam_, xs_] := Module[{n = Length[vals] - 1, c},
   c = N[(Range[n] - 1/2)/n];
   vals[[1]] + s[lam Outer[Subtract, N[xs], c]] . Differences[N[vals]]];
nodes[n_] := N[Range[0, n]/n];
xsFine = Range[0., 1., 0.0005];
supErrS[s_, fun_, n_, lam_] :=
  Max@Abs[fun[xsFine] - stairOn[s, fun[nodes[n]], lam, xsFine]];
(* check: stairOn agrees with stair of the main notebook, c.8 *)
stair[fun_, n_, lam_][x_] := fun[0] +
   Sum[(fun[k/n] - fun[(k - 1)/n]) *
     LogisticSigmoid[lam (x - (k - 1/2)/n)], {k, 1, n}];
Max@Abs[stairOn[LogisticSigmoid, f[nodes[10]], 200, {0.13, 0.5, 0.77}] -
   (stair[f, 10, 200] /@ {0.13, 0.5, 0.77})]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:=",ExpressionUUID->"10aa1562-6728-40c6-b850-ba43145c569e"],

Cell[BoxData["2.220446049250313`*^-16"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0037954181776533`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[24]=",ExpressionUUID->"8b4cd674-aed5-4805-b716-b58d29c817e0"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
1. Problem 1: the staircase with arctan and algebraic sigmoids\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4a60a601-92dd-4a87-8f42-eb9ecf4ce8fb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Problem 1. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Repeat the staircase experiment of section 4 (Table M3) with the arctan and \
algebraic sigmoids. Why do you need a larger \[Lambda] for the same error?"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4479be9c-9b75-49f8-a36a-332f188c3c5c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The three S-shapes and their tails", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"0bfcbd71-d9ba-4028-b5f4-e00d47d9fa6a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The three functions are the logistic \[Sigma](t) = 1/(1 + ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["e", 
    RowBox[{"-", "t"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2733af97-41f4-4040-9d74-ba0cebc64f6c"],
 "), the arctan sigmoid 1/2 + arctan(t)/\[Pi] and the algebraic sigmoid (1 + \
t/\[Sqrt](1 + ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["t", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "160b62dd-a2a8-4f6a-a5fe-6fc3d9f095db"],
 "))/2. All three are sigmoidal in the sense of Eq. (M1) and all three are \
symmetric, \[Sigma](-t) = 1 - \[Sigma](t). What separates them is how fast \
they reach their limits. Write T(u) = 1 - \[Sigma](u) for the tail, the \
distance from the limit 1 at u > 0. By symmetry the same T(u) is the distance \
from the limit 0 at -u. As u \[RightArrow] \[Infinity],"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9de1a088-092d-4c39-80bd-be54ead6aa13"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"1", "-", 
     RowBox[{"\[Sigma]", 
      RowBox[{"(", "u", ")"}]}]}], "\[Tilde]", 
    RowBox[{"{", GridBox[{
       {
        StyleBox[
         SuperscriptBox["e", 
          RowBox[{"-", "u"}]],
         ScriptLevel->0], 
        StyleBox["logistic",
         ScriptLevel->0,
         FontSlant->"Plain"]},
       {
        StyleBox[
         FractionBox["1", 
          RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "u"}]],
         ScriptLevel->0], 
        StyleBox["arctan",
         ScriptLevel->0,
         FontSlant->"Plain"]},
       {
        StyleBox[
         FractionBox["1", 
          RowBox[{"4", 
           SuperscriptBox["u", "2"]}]],
         ScriptLevel->0], 
        StyleBox["algebraic",
         ScriptLevel->0,
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}
      },
      GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1}}, "Rows" -> {{0.8}}}]}], "   ", 
    RowBox[{"u", "\[Rule]", "\[Infinity]"}]}], "        ", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "1.1", ")"}],
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"ca95a321-b50f-43bc-9ee3-1cc2a0608598"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The logistic tail is exponential; the other two are algebraic, and the \
arctan tail is the slowest of all: at u = 1000 it is still 3 \[Times] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "4"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "113902df-655a-428c-98ba-ba3cce6c3154"],
 ". Solving T(u) = \[Eta] for u gives the steepness at which each function is \
within \[Eta] of its limit:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cc4d3c39-51d6-4dae-8ef7-2c1180b3e701"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["u", "\[Eta]"], "="}], 
    RowBox[{"{", GridBox[{
       {
        StyleBox[
         RowBox[{"log", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           FractionBox[
            RowBox[{"1", "-", "\[Eta]"}], "\[Eta]"], ")"}]}],
         ScriptLevel->0], 
        StyleBox["logistic",
         ScriptLevel->0,
         FontSlant->"Plain"]},
       {
        StyleBox[
         RowBox[{"cot", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "\[Eta]"}], ")"}]}],
         ScriptLevel->0], 
        StyleBox["arctan",
         ScriptLevel->0,
         FontSlant->"Plain"]},
       {
        StyleBox[
         FractionBox[
          RowBox[{"1", "-", 
           RowBox[{"2", "\[Eta]"}]}], 
          RowBox[{"2", 
           SqrtBox[
            RowBox[{"\[Eta]", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"1", "-", "\[Eta]"}], ")"}]}]]}]],
         ScriptLevel->0], 
        StyleBox["algebraic",
         ScriptLevel->0,
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}
      },
      GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1}}, "Rows" -> {{0.8}}}]}]}], "        ", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "1.2", ")"}],
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"606920c3-bf6f-4326-ba27-2e2f8c820de0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For \[Eta] = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "6"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2c3e130d-4fdc-45b8-9eb9-7c7836ae22a3"],
 " the logistic needs u \[TildeTilde] 14, the algebraic sigmoid u \
\[TildeTilde] 500 and the arctan sigmoid u \[TildeTilde] 318000: the logistic \
grows like ln(1/\[Eta]), the algebraic like 1/(2\[Sqrt]\[Eta]) and the arctan \
like 1/(\[Pi]\[Eta])."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e76aa972-2a2c-466a-b6fd-b28d02003a3f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Figure 1.1. Left: the three S-shapes. Right: their tails 1 - \[Sigma](u) on \
log-log axes, with the leading terms 1/(\[Pi]u) and 1/(4",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["u", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a0d0dfb4-ca65-47e3-a854-bf7643636c52"],
 ") of Eq. (1.1) dashed. The logistic tail falls off the bottom of the plot \
near u = 18."
}], "Caption",
 FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"610a7122-e70c-46fd-ba32-20681a4ec16e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(*c.1.1*)
sig3 = <|\"logistic\" -> LogisticSigmoid,
   \"arctan\" -> (1/2 + ArcTan[#]/Pi &),
   \"algebraic\" -> ((1 + #/Sqrt[1 + #^2])/2 &)|>;
(* the tail 1 - \[Sigma](u): distance to the limit 1. All three satisfy
   \[Sigma](-u) = 1 - \[Sigma](u), so \[Sigma](-u) gives the tail without \
round-off *)
tail[k_][u_] := sig3[k][-u];
figure[{{
   Plot[Evaluate[Through[Values[sig3][t]]], {t, -10, 10},
    PlotRange -> {-0.02, 1.02}, AxesLabel -> {\"t\", \"\[Sigma](t)\"},
    PlotLegends -> Placed[LineLegend[Keys[sig3],
       LabelStyle -> Directive[figFont - 3]], Below],
    Evaluate@panel[PlotLabel -> \"1.1a. three S-shapes\"]],
   Quiet@LogLogPlot[Evaluate@Join[Table[tail[k][u], {k, Keys[sig3]}],
      {1/(Pi u), 1/(4 u^2)}], {u, 1, 1000},
    PlotRange -> {10^-8, 1}, Ticks -> {{1, 10, 100, 1000}, Automatic},
    PlotStyle -> Join[ColorData[97] /@ {1, 2, 3},
      Table[Directive[Black, Dashed], 2]],
    Evaluate@panel[PlotLabel -> \"1.1b. tail 1 - \[Sigma](u)\"]]}},
 \"Figure 1.1. The three S-shapes and their tails\"]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[25]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1a43106e-0fbc-41c7-b64f-0d2d2ab82259"],

