Cell["\<\
The shape in Figure 1.4 has a name. With T(u) \[TildeTilde] 1/(\[Pi]u), Eq. \
(1.4) becomes, for large N, -(1/(\[Pi]\[Lambda])) times the principal-value \
integral of f\[Prime](s)/(x - s) over [0, 1]: a truncated Hilbert transform \
of f\[Prime]. The Hilbert transform of a cosine is a sine, and f\[Prime] is \
dominated by 2\[Pi] cos(2\[Pi]x). A tail as heavy as 1/u reaches every step \
of the staircase.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7f3d737d-7112-4a57-a20c-239adf6fba97"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Answer", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"9b613d62-57f1-42ef-b527-063c311c2338"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With \[Lambda] = 20 N, as in Table M3, the three S-shapes give almost the \
same sup-norm error, because the error is set by the coarseness of the \
staircase. The S-shape matters in how quickly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["G", "N"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a218f4c3-4616-4073-aba9-418e8e406105"],
 " approaches the ideal staircase of hard steps, which is the limit used in \
Cybenko's proof. A sigmoid reaches its limits at the rate of its tail, Eq. \
(1.1): exponentially for the logistic, like 1/",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["u", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "fe76ddda-a9aa-4e6b-85a4-28adfce87695"],
 " for the algebraic and like 1/u for the arctan sigmoid. Each step leaks its \
tail into the neighbouring nodes, Eq. (1.4), so the slower the tail, the \
larger \[Lambda] must be for the same leakage, Eq. (1.5) and Table 1.4. For a \
leakage of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "3"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5925da82-4f35-4f3b-9c76-fb92891e8e33"],
 " at N = 20: \[Lambda] \[TildeTilde] 235, 401 and 6279."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"773e2920-f436-459e-ba6c-116ac69c7850"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. Problem 2: a sigmoidal function that is not monotone", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"08800f44-9412-4614-a7d1-6fc793850d03"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Problem 2. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Try a non-monotone function such as \[Sigma](t) + sin(t) exp(-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["t", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3c580fd4-6924-4779-bd2f-4ed20a17ac0d"],
 "). Is it sigmoidal in the sense of Eq. (M1), and does the staircase still \
converge?"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1edfb6d4-bde3-4b83-a583-489a705e2706"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Is it sigmoidal?", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"f4224270-1abb-4280-b279-6f5f5bf8fbc6"],

Cell["Write s for the new function:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f5fded7c-18d5-41f5-8f2c-c0afb703d577"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"s", 
      RowBox[{"(", "t", ")"}]}], "=", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Sigma]", 
       RowBox[{"(", "t", ")"}]}], "+", 
      RowBox[{"sin", " ", "t", " ", 
       SuperscriptBox["e", 
        RowBox[{"-", 
         SuperscriptBox["t", "2"]}]]}]}]}], 
    RowBox[{",", "    "}], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox["lim", 
       RowBox[{"t", "\[Rule]", 
        RowBox[{"-", "\[Infinity]"}]}]], " ", 
      RowBox[{"s", 
       RowBox[{"(", "t", ")"}]}]}], "=", "0"}], 
    RowBox[{",", "  "}], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox["lim", 
       RowBox[{"t", "\[Rule]", 
        RowBox[{"+", "\[Infinity]"}]}]], " ", 
      RowBox[{"s", 
       RowBox[{"(", "t", ")"}]}]}], "=", "1"}]}], "        ", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "2.1", ")"}],
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"8f612624-d07e-48c9-8453-010d77237b2a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Since |sin(t) exp(-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["t", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "550b87d2-087a-47ae-b0eb-69e426b7959e"],
 ")| \[LessEqual] exp(-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["t", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "468ab53c-d0e4-453c-84fa-9f352d2e8592"],
 ") \[RightArrow] 0, the added term disappears at both ends and the limits \
are those of \[Sigma]: 0 and 1. That is all Eq. (M1) asks for, so s is \
sigmoidal. It is also continuous, and it keeps the symmetry s(-t) = 1 - s(t), \
because sin is odd. But it is not monotone. Its derivative changes sign four \
times in (-4, 4). s rises above 1, to 1.068 at t = 0.784, and by symmetry \
dips below 0, to -0.068 at t = -0.784."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9c09b810-cfe2-4b93-9521-e9fe5e35b723"],

Cell["\<\
Table 2.1. Properties of s, computed symbolically and numerically.\
\>", "Caption",
 FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"36ad85b2-009b-48ea-b2d9-9f952c70bdcb"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(*c.2.1*)
s2[t_] := LogisticSigmoid[t] + Sin[t] Exp[-t^2];
{tMax, tMin} = t /. {Last[#], First[#]} &@
    NSolve[D[s2[t], t] == 0 && -1 < t < 1, t];
table[{
  {\"property\", \"value\"},
  {\"limit t \[RightArrow] -\[Infinity]\", Limit[s2[t], t -> -Infinity]},
  {\"limit t \[RightArrow] +\[Infinity]\", Limit[s2[t], t -> Infinity]},
  {\"sigmoidal, Eq. (M1)?\", \"yes\"},
  {\"\[Sigma](-t) = 1 - \[Sigma](t)?\", FullSimplify[s2[-t] == 1 - s2[t]]},
  {\"largest value\", Row[{NumberForm[s2[tMax], 4], \" at t = \",
     NumberForm[tMax, 4]}]},
  {\"smallest value\", Row[{NumberForm[s2[tMin], 4], \" at t = \",
     NumberForm[tMin, 4]}]},
  {\"zeros of \[Sigma]' in (-4, 4)\", NumberForm[t /. NSolve[
       D[s2[t], t] == 0 && -4 < t < 4, t], 4]},
  {\"monotone?\", \"no: \[Sigma]' < 0 on two intervals\"}}, \"Table 2.1\"]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[64]:=",ExpressionUUID->"967b9c74-8d92-4a83-a39e-584bdb6e2770"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TemplateBox[{
   TagBox[
    GridBox[{{"\"property\"", "\"value\""}, {
      "\"limit t \[RightArrow] -\[Infinity]\"", "0"}, {
      "\"limit t \[RightArrow] +\[Infinity]\"", "1"}, {
      "\"sigmoidal, Eq. (M1)?\"", "\"yes\""}, {
      "\"\[Sigma](-t) = 1 - \[Sigma](t)?\"", "True"}, {"\"largest value\"", 
       TemplateBox[{
         TagBox[
          InterpretationBox[
           StyleBox["\"1.068\"", ShowStringCharacters -> False], 
