Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Which theorem?", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"b343e559-1492-4ce9-a482-f4ce7bfa7eca"],

Cell["\<\
Theorem M8 (Leshno, Lin, Pinkus and Schocken) explains it. One-hidden-layer \
networks are universal if and only if the activation is not a polynomial. Its \
\"only if\" direction is exactly Eq. (3.1): with a polynomial activation of \
degree k the network can only make polynomials of degree at most k, a \
finite-dimensional space, which cannot approximate every continuous function.\
\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"34621524-ab29-4a3c-a000-10fd34f749ce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Theorems M1\[Dash]M4 of Cybenko do not apply, since ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["t", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7865033e-5e4f-490e-8983-8c7dec3d0790"],
 " is not sigmoidal: both its limits are +\[Infinity]. But a theorem that \
does not apply says nothing about failure; Cybenko gives sufficient \
conditions only."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"16b4575d-e799-4c7f-b63b-9a149028fe2c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Theorems M6 and M7 also do not apply (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["t", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ede4415b-f246-4ad9-bc33-db6d01a5cf7e"],
 " is neither squashing nor bounded), and they too only give sufficient \
conditions. Only Theorem M8 is an \"if and only if\"."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"82bd827b-889d-415f-93ba-fbdf46b317d1"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Answer", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"f0e62004-73f2-4bb7-943c-9eb24a1b73bc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With \[Sigma](t) = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["t", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "37d75afb-527f-464f-b401-d3a9cef0a685"],
 " every network is a quadratic polynomial, Eq. (3.1), whatever N is. The \
least-squares error stops at that of the best quadratic, which for this g is \
the zero polynomial with RMS error 1/2. With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["t", "3"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ff7984ab-8a44-4622-a9d6-6013b3a0713e"],
 " it stops at the best cubic, RMS 0.331. Theorem M8 of Leshno, Lin, Pinkus \
and Schocken explains this: one hidden layer is universal exactly when the \
activation is not a polynomial."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"82b0039b-16fd-471c-b3be-5878c86a8eb9"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4. Problem 4: x y z as a Kolmogorov superposition", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"cc4ce0bf-eb21-4c98-9a07-63c440b79f45"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Problem 4. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Write x y z as a superposition in the form of Eq. (M8), using one-variable \
functions and addition, valid for positive x, y, z."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b72c5d4f-e119-4b38-8e95-d9ebae22f440"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The solution", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"377ba2c1-6da5-47a7-a830-d197fe9d75c5"],

Cell["\<\
The logarithm turns a product into a sum, and the exponential turns it back:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1b4c016e-e184-4cfe-b157-9461a22a3e02"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"x", "y", "z"}], "=", 
    RowBox[{"exp", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ln", " ", "x"}], "+", 
       RowBox[{"ln", " ", "y"}], "+", 
       RowBox[{"ln", " ", "z"}]}], ")"}]}], 
    RowBox[{",", "    "}], 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", "y", ",", "z", ">", "0"}]}], "        ", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "4.1", ")"}],
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"a3070f11-01ac-4894-93c9-225b4d239989"],

Cell["\<\
This has the shape of Eq. (M8) with n = 3: inner functions applied to each \
variable separately, their sum, then one outer function. Eq. (M8) has 2n + 1 \
= 7 branches, q = 0, ..., 6; we need only the first and set the outer \
function of the others to zero:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c6c5eb02-d136-4bab-84cf-400c5d3bfe5c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "0"], "=", "exp"}], 
    RowBox[{",", "  "}], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
      RowBox[{"p", ",", "0"}]], "=", "ln"}], 
    RowBox[{",", "  "}], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "q"], "=", "0"}], "  ", 
    StyleBox["for",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "  ", 
    RowBox[{"q", "=", "1", ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", "6"}]}], "        ", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "4.2", ")"}],
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"caad15ca-1de7-4ee5-a42a-d087fdc941f9"],

Cell["\<\
The inner functions are continuous and increasing, as in Kolmogorov's \
theorem, but they are not universal: they were chosen for this f. \
Kolmogorov's theorem promises universal inner functions that work for every \
f, at the price of being very rough. Here a smooth, special-purpose choice is \
enough. Positivity is needed because ln is defined only for positive \
arguments: at x = 0 the inner value would be -\[Infinity].\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"92337589-64c2-43d3-a558-3e29da30fa5e"],

Cell["Two checks: the identities used, symbolically.", "Caption",
 FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"f3e731dc-45b4-4756-8e79-6c04d5788600"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(*c.4.1*)
(* the two identities behind the solution *)
<|\"exp(ln x + ln y + ln z) = x y z, for x, y, z > 0\" ->
   FullSimplify[Exp[Log[x] + Log[y] + Log[z]] == x y z,
    x > 0 && y > 0 && z > 0],
  \"four cubes, Eq. (4.3), for all real x, y, z\" ->
   Expand[((x + y + z)^3 - (x + y - z)^3 - (x - y + z)^3 +
        (x - y - z)^3)/24] == x y z|>\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[129]:=",ExpressionUUID->"0b7f3620-782a-4ff7-a6fb-00d3c80514c2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"exp(ln x + ln y + ln z) = x y z, for x, y, z > 0\"\>", "\[Rule]",
     "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"four cubes, Eq. (4.3), for all real x, y, z\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    "True"}]}], "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.003795422543251*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[131]=",ExpressionUUID->"9c22b66f-2632-48fc-b410-ff2bcfe6cc14"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Eq. (M8) for n = 3 with the functions of Eq. (4.2), checked symbolically and \
on 10000 random points of (0, 1]\.b3.\
\>", "Caption",
 FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"a85b0ada-d3e0-4767-b3b9-844afef1f178"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(*c.4.2*)
(* Eq. (8) of the main notebook for n = 3: 2n + 1 = 7 branches,
   q = 0, ..., 6. Branch 0 carries the product, the others are zero *)
psi[p_, q_] := If[q == 0, Log, (0 &)];   (* inner functions \[Psi]_{p,q} *)
Phi[q_] := If[q == 0, Exp, (0 &)];       (* outer functions \[CapitalPhi]_q \
*)
kolmogorov[xs_List] := Sum[
   Phi[q][Sum[psi[p, q][xs[[p]]], {p, 1, 3}]], {q, 0, 6}];
SeedRandom[4];
pts = RandomReal[{0.001, 1}, {10000, 3}];
<|\"symbolic\" -> FullSimplify[kolmogorov[{x, y, z}] == x y z,
    x > 0 && y > 0 && z > 0],
  \"largest relative error on 10000 random points\" ->
   Max@Abs[(kolmogorov /@ pts)/(Times @@@ pts) - 1]|>\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[132]:=",ExpressionUUID->"84b57fe6-6e4a-405d-97c3-ee5b37b64fd0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"symbolic\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"largest relative error on 10000 random points\"\>", "\[Rule]",
     "1.7763568394002505`*^-15"}]}], "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.003795422708902*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[139]=",ExpressionUUID->"805e37ec-4c5d-4284-a0f1-e67d38f68242"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Figure 4.1. Eq. (M8) as a network for n = 3, in the style of Figure M8. All \
seven branches are drawn; only the branch q = 0 (black edges, red nodes) does \
any work, and the other six have outer function 0.\
\>", "Caption",
 FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"59a31ff0-d913-471d-8cc5-d7850d0ae540"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(*c.4.3*)
(* Eq. (8) drawn as a network for n = 3, in the style of Figure M8.
   Black and red: the branch q = 0 that does the work. Gray: the six
   branches whose outer function is zero *)
psiV[p_, q_] := Subscript[\"\[Psi]\", ToString[p] <> ToString[q]];
edges = Flatten@{
    Table[DirectedEdge[Subscript[\"x\", p], psiV[p, q]], {p, 3}, {q, 0, 6}],
    Table[DirectedEdge[psiV[p, q], Subscript[\"\[CapitalPhi]\", q]], {p, 3}, \
{q, 0, 6}],
    Table[DirectedEdge[Subscript[\"\[CapitalPhi]\", q], \"f\"], {q, 0, 6}]};
active = Flatten@{
    Table[DirectedEdge[Subscript[\"x\", p], psiV[p, 0]], {p, 3}],
    Table[DirectedEdge[psiV[p, 0], Subscript[\"\[CapitalPhi]\", 0]], {p, 3}],
    DirectedEdge[Subscript[\"\[CapitalPhi]\", 0], \"f\"]};
(* one row per inner function, grouped by branch q *)
yPsi[p_, q_] := If[q == 0, -2 p, -(4 q + p + 4)];
coords = Join[
   Flatten@Table[psiV[p, q] -> {2, yPsi[p, q]}, {p, 3}, {q, 0, 6}],
   Table[Subscript[\"\[CapitalPhi]\", q] -> {4, yPsi[2, q]}, {q, 0, 6}],
   Table[Subscript[\"x\", p] -> {0, -(8 p + 1)}, {p, 3}], {\"f\" -> {6, -14}}];
Graph[edges, VertexCoordinates -> coords,
 EdgeStyle -> Join[(# -> Directive[Black, Thick] &) /@ active,
   (# -> Directive[GrayLevel[0.82]] &) /@ Complement[edges, active]],
 VertexStyle -> Join[(# -> Red &) /@ {psiV[1, 0], psiV[2, 0], psiV[3, 0],
     Subscript[\"\[CapitalPhi]\", 0]}, Flatten@Table[psiV[p, q] -> \
GrayLevel[0.8],
     {p, 3}, {q, 6}], Table[Subscript[\"\[CapitalPhi]\", q] -> \
GrayLevel[0.8], {q, 6}]],
 VertexSize -> 0.6,
 VertexLabels -> Join[
   Table[psiV[p, 0] -> Placed[\"ln\", Above], {p, 3}],
   {Subscript[\"\[CapitalPhi]\", 0] -> Placed[\"exp\", Above]},
   Table[Subscript[\"\[CapitalPhi]\", q] -> Placed[Style[\"0\", Gray], \
Above], {q, 6}],
   (# -> Placed[#, Above] &) /@ {Subscript[\"x\", 1], Subscript[\"x\", 2],
     Subscript[\"x\", 3], \"f\"}],
 VertexLabelStyle -> Directive[Black, figFont - 2],
 ImageSize -> {wFull, Automatic}, AspectRatio -> 1.1,
 PlotLabel -> Style[\"Figure 4.1. x y z as a Kolmogorov network\",
   figFont]]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[140]:=",ExpressionUUID->"19e26e70-faea-4118-9e16-45ab02d8cb4b"],

