}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The comparison makes the point of section 4 of the main notebook concrete. \
The staircase is a proof device: it shows that some weights exist. Trained \
weights are far better: 8 trained units reach an error of 8 \[Times] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "4"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "25fc9560-f9ff-4f2b-9baf-259374c46333"],
 ", while the staircase needs 80 units for 0.028 and would need thousands to \
match."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bbfb6e77-90b8-4bd6-8123-b311ce486a62"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Answer", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"3d12575d-3274-409c-b3e8-396a7fc59338"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "By the path rule of Eq. (M5): \[PartialD]G/\[PartialD]",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "j"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3cdb11f2-d4f2-475d-8b92-4fcc908df45c"],
 " = \[Sigma](",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["z", "j"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1205d464-2d76-461a-b36b-e688e29fc66a"],
 "), Eq. (6.1), and \[PartialD]G/\[PartialD]",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["y", "ji"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ba689d06-6f7f-48e4-b28e-0dd254bc3d3d"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "j"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8512a563-465c-480c-a920-03dc4ed87f2d"],
 " \[Sigma]\[Prime](",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["z", "j"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ff3d115b-2a93-4507-8ab8-d8545139de00"],
 ") ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "i"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "74c1bf93-3f05-48d5-b577-16addf9556e6"],
 ", Eq. (6.3), with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["z", "j"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8d9e99e7-df86-4da8-866d-8ee2e530ba0a"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["y", "j"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "33d96a99-0238-4adc-8d19-ea44c0d61214"],
 "\[CenterDot]x + ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Theta]", "j"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0b48e55e-50c3-4b2e-b80f-5f07c741a85d"],
 "; also \[PartialD]G/\[PartialD]",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Theta]", "j"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "20033a52-8544-4bf8-8e9a-3a7fe52843f6"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "j"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "edd3e8a1-c83f-454d-a613-f41e532aab8a"],
 " \[Sigma]\[Prime](",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["z", "j"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "48bfb0d4-736a-4999-a064-795bc9b2b11a"],
 "), Eq. (6.2). They agree with D to 7 \[Times] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "18"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5d946b6b-084a-4cf1-98d6-6120a313e69a"],
 " (Table 6.1). Built into the loss gradient Eq. (6.4), they agree with \
finite differences to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "10"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7f1a0604-445c-4966-816c-0157ee4b8fbc"],
 " and train an 8-unit network to a maximum error of 8 \[Times] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "4"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "caa4c62a-a53e-47d3-b7b2-490f4e12522f"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"575c4f4a-54eb-4742-8698-6db6529245e2"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["7. Problem 7: rates from the modulus of continuity", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"719eb3cb-8e71-46f5-a9ef-620de0efadf9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Problem 7. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Run the staircase of section 4 on x sin(1/x) (with value 0 at 0) and on the \
Cantor staircase of Figure M9. Predict the rate of convergence from the \
modulus of continuity, Eq. (M12), before you measure it."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3e4b97d8-9a7a-4bd1-a30a-e7e56039573f"],

Cell["\<\
Figure 7.1. The two targets, with zooms. x sin(1/x) oscillates infinitely \
often near 0 with amplitude x; the Cantor staircase C repeats itself at every \
scale.\
\>", "Caption",
 FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"408f5eda-7959-4be4-ad13-a9247a737c0a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(*c.7.1*)
(* the two functions, safe on whole arrays (x sin(1/x) is 0 at 0) *)
xsin[x_] := x Sin[1/(x + 10.^-300)];
cantor[x_] := CantorStaircase[x];
targets = <|\"x sin(1/x)\" -> xsin, \"Cantor\" -> cantor|>;
figure[{{
   Plot[xsin[x], {x, 0, 1}, PlotPoints -> 2000, PlotRange -> All,
    Evaluate@panel[PlotLabel -> \"7.1a. x sin(1/x)\"]],
   Plot[xsin[x], {x, 0, 0.1}, PlotPoints -> 2000, PlotRange -> All,
    Ticks -> {{0.05, 0.1}, Automatic},
    Evaluate@panel[PlotLabel -> \"7.1b. zoom, 0 \[LessEqual] x \[LessEqual] \
0.1\"]]},
  {Plot[cantor[x], {x, 0, 1},
    Evaluate@panel[PlotLabel -> \"7.1c. Cantor staircase\"]],
   Plot[cantor[x], {x, 0, 1/9}, Ticks -> {{1/27, 2/27, 1/9}, Automatic},
    Evaluate@panel[PlotLabel -> \"7.1d. zoom, 0 \[LessEqual] x \[LessEqual] \
1/9\"]]}},
 \"Figure 7.1. The two targets\"]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[233]:=",ExpressionUUID->"48f3a6f1-d188-47aa-8123-29b80b4d8d8e"],

